results runner: End User Licence

Copyright (c) 2026 Swimming South Australia Inc. (SwimmingSA). All rights reserved.

This repository holds the built, ready-to-run versions of results runner and the
files the app uses to check for a newer version. It does not hold the source code,
which is not published.

1. What you may do

   You may download results runner and run it on computers you own or control,
   for swimming administration: ratifying records, running meets and carnivals,
   and the related reporting the app provides. This applies to SwimmingSA, its
   member clubs, officials and volunteers, and to other swimming bodies with
   SwimmingSA's agreement.

   You may make copies as needed to install and back up the app.

2. What you may not do

   You may not sell, rent, sublicense or otherwise distribute results runner
   to anyone else. Point them to this repository instead.

   You may not modify, decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer the app, or
   extract its source code or assets, except where the law expressly allows it
   regardless of this clause.

   You may not remove or alter any copyright, trademark or version notice in
   the app or its files.

   You may not use the SwimmingSA name, logo or brand assets bundled with the
   app for any purpose other than running the app.

3. Data

   Everything results runner reads and writes stays on your computer or in the
   folder you choose. SwimmingSA does not receive it through the app. Records,
   results and personal details you process with the app remain your
   responsibility under the privacy rules that apply to you.

4. Updates

   The app may check this repository for a newer version and tell you one is
   available. Downloading it is your choice. SwimmingSA may change or withdraw
   releases at any time.

5. No warranty

   results runner is provided as is, without warranty of any kind, express or
   implied, including fitness for a particular purpose. Records ratified with it
   remain subject to the rules and approvals of the governing body concerned;
   the app assists that process and does not replace it.

6. Limitation of liability

   To the extent the law allows, SwimmingSA is not liable for any loss or damage
   arising from the use of, or inability to use, results runner, including lost
   or incorrect data. Nothing in this licence excludes rights you have under the
   Australian Consumer Law that cannot be excluded.

7. Ending the licence

   This licence ends if you breach it. You must then delete every copy of the
   app you hold. Sections 3 to 6 survive.

8. Governing law

   This licence is governed by the laws of South Australia, Australia.

